Package: tanmai
Title: Read Chess Positions from Screenshots, FEN, PGN and Video
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Tanmay", "Chanda", email = "81738153+tenmeh@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads a chess position from a screenshot of a board, a FEN
    string, a PGN file, or a recording of a game being played, and returns it
    as a tidy data frame - one row per position, or one row per ply for a
    game. Recognition reports how confident it is rather than silently
    guessing. With a 'Stockfish' engine installed, games can additionally be
    evaluated, scored for accuracy, and searched for the moves that decided
    them; without one, everything that reads a position still works.
URL: https://github.com/tenmeh/tanmai-r
BugReports: https://github.com/tenmeh/tanmai-r/issues
